  "changes": [
    "Read shows files as native does: lossy UTF-8 (UTF-16 too), BOM aside, CRLF as LF, also through the large-file range helper; results name the file as the call did",
    "Edit keeps UTF-16LE (by BOM), UTF-8 BOM and CRLF endings; strings taken as given; empty old_string creates a missing file or fills an empty one, otherwise 'Cannot create new file - file already exists.'; native not-found and multiple-match messages",
    "unread files may be edited or written, as natively (Edit marks contentNotInModelContext); a file read and changed since is refused with native's message; NotebookEdit still requires a Read",
    "Write to a directory fails with native's message",
    "before writing an unread or new file, its prior state is recorded, so a retry after a lost write is refused instead of applied twice or overwriting a later change"
  ],
  "gates": {
    "source_tests": 191,
    "check_compact": "passed on the feature tree, on merge fbaa715c and on merge f87dd16b (both brought Rust changes from origin/main); the plugin sources are identical across them",
    "native_review": "4 read-only Codex review rounds; fixed: CR doubling from normalizing edit strings (native takes them as given, measured), unbounded originalFile, range-read BOM and CR boundaries, the range helper's strict decoding, lost-write retries for unread and new files; the last reported none",
    "release_note": "the post-signing gate rebuilt dist's unbound release envelope; the preserved signed envelope was restored and re-verified before publication"
  },
